1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,709
What if your computer could understand a task, carry it out, and show you proof?

2
00:00:05,709 --> 00:00:10,607
Meet Custodian: an offline Windows assistant built around a simple principle.

3
00:00:10,607 --> 00:00:13,050
Every supported action should be accountable.

4
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:20,054
Finding the right files, organizing a project, and checking every result takes time.

5
00:00:20,054 --> 00:00:25,361
Automation helps, but a confident answer is not evidence that your files are correct, or

6
00:00:25,361 --> 00:00:27,050
that your work is protected.

7
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:31,947
Custodian brings those tasks into one conversation.

8
00:00:31,947 --> 00:00:34,071
Cubby is its on-screen companion.

9
00:00:34,071 --> 00:00:39,734
You describe the outcome, the local model proposes a supported plan, and native controls

10
00:00:39,734 --> 00:00:42,050
determine what can actually execute.

11
00:00:43,550 --> 00:00:46,319
An open-weight Qwen model runs on the computer.

12
00:00:46,319 --> 00:00:50,329
Supported local workflows do not need a cloud account or an upload.

13
00:00:50,329 --> 00:00:55,514
The model interprets the request; it does not receive unrestricted authority over

14
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:56,027
Windows.

15
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:03,836
The request becomes a bounded program: discover, select, approve, execute, and verify.

16
00:01:03,836 --> 00:01:07,921
Native checks bind the plan to real locations and allowed operations.

17
00:01:07,921 --> 00:01:12,050
Unsupported or ambiguous requests must be refused or clarified.

18
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:15,508
Consider a project handoff.

19
00:01:15,508 --> 00:01:21,049
Set a private location, then ask Custodian to copy the permitted project files to a

20
00:01:21,049 --> 00:01:22,317
chosen destination.

21
00:01:22,317 --> 00:01:27,477
Discovery can cover permitted local drives and ordinary folders, rather than just

22
00:01:27,477 --> 00:01:28,942
Documents or Downloads.

23
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:35,630
Before the effect, a native approval preview identifies the selected files, destination,

24
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:37,593
exclusions, and recovery behavior.

25
00:01:37,593 --> 00:01:40,470
Optional standing permissions support bounded routines.

26
00:01:40,470 --> 00:01:45,050
A changed source, a conflict, or missing authority prevents an unsafe substitution.

27
00:01:46,550 --> 00:01:50,752
Execution produces evidence, not just a success message.

28
00:01:50,752 --> 00:01:54,362
File identities and content checks help verify the result.

29
00:01:54,362 --> 00:01:56,960
The task retains receipts and progress.

30
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:02,519
If a required check fails, that failure stays visible instead of becoming a completion

31
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:02,907
claim.

32
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:09,912
For supported operations, receipts provide a path to undo and recovery inspection.

33
00:02:09,912 --> 00:02:14,352
If you edit an output afterwards, undo must preserve that later work.

34
00:02:14,352 --> 00:02:19,549
After an interruption, recovery inspects the evidence rather than blindly replaying

35
00:02:19,549 --> 00:02:20,050
effects.

36
00:02:21,550 --> 00:02:25,268
Private paths and protected locations are checked by native controls.

37
00:02:25,268 --> 00:02:29,529
Application exclusions provide a separate boundary for supported app workflows.

38
00:02:29,529 --> 00:02:32,288
Stop and revocation are execution controls.

39
00:02:32,288 --> 00:02:36,050
Document text and model suggestions cannot grant themselves permission.

40
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:42,768
The prototype also has narrow, version-qualified Visual Studio Code and Excel workflows.

41
00:02:42,768 --> 00:02:48,461
Native checks have exercised text editing, spreadsheet recalculation, save and reopen,

42
00:02:48,461 --> 00:02:51,308
source preservation, publication, and undo.

43
00:02:51,308 --> 00:02:55,050
These are specific adapters, not universal desktop control.

44
00:02:56,550 --> 00:03:00,113
A Tauri and React interface connects to a Rust execution core.

45
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:05,068
Authenticated communication, supervised workers, deadlines, and durable journals support

46
00:03:05,068 --> 00:03:05,801
the boundary.

47
00:03:05,801 --> 00:03:10,562
The security claim is controlled, verified execution within supported scope, not

48
00:03:10,562 --> 00:03:12,050
immunity to every threat.

49
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:18,328
Recorded checks include a twenty-nine-check desktop baseline, real editor and Excel

50
00:03:18,328 --> 00:03:20,861
workflows, and nine editor safety scenarios.

51
00:03:20,861 --> 00:03:22,349
These are measured subsets.

52
00:03:22,349 --> 00:03:26,795
They do not establish complete-product security, unrestricted automation, or finished

53
00:03:26,795 --> 00:03:28,050
installation acceptance.

54
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:34,730
Next come stronger model reliability, repeated packaged validation, and clean offline

55
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:35,523
installation.

56
00:03:35,523 --> 00:03:40,262
Archives, backup, document, and media workflows expand after native integration and

57
00:03:40,262 --> 00:03:41,004
verification.

58
00:03:41,004 --> 00:03:44,629
Laya remains experimental, not an active security control.

59
00:03:44,629 --> 00:03:47,050
Online capabilities remain future scope.

60
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:49,490
Custodian.

61
00:03:49,490 --> 00:03:50,787
Local intelligence.

62
00:03:50,787 --> 00:03:52,127
Verifiable action.

63
00:03:52,127 --> 00:03:53,159
A path back.

64
00:03:53,159 --> 00:03:54,536
Our ambition is broad.

65
00:03:54,536 --> 00:03:56,030
Our standard is evidence.

66
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:59,050
Help us build an assistant people can trust with real work.
